1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,730
What's today's video about? It's about various procedures. They can be tricky, right?

2
00:00:08,730 --> 00:00:23,015
At some point in the video, a question will appear in Japanese. If you catch it, leave a comment! Scene 1: Residence Registration Procedure

3
00:00:23,015 --> 00:00:25,055
Excuse me.

4
00:00:25,078 --> 00:00:28,645
I just arrived in Japan.

5
00:00:28,668 --> 00:00:32,101
I'd like to register my address.

6
00:00:32,124 --> 00:00:34,324
Welcome.

7
00:00:34,347 --> 00:00:37,044
Welcome to the ward office.

8
00:00:37,067 --> 00:00:40,001
You're here for a new address registration, right?

9
00:00:40,024 --> 00:00:42,763
Yes, that's right.

10
00:00:42,786 --> 00:00:45,753
I'm really nervous.

11
00:00:45,776 --> 00:00:48,176
Don't worry, it's okay.

12
00:00:48,199 --> 00:00:53,888
First, may I see your residence card and passport?

13
00:00:53,911 --> 00:00:56,525
Yes, I have them.

14
00:00:56,548 --> 00:01:00,243
I'll take them out of my bag.

15
00:01:00,267 --> 00:01:02,200
Here you go.

16
00:01:02,223 --> 00:01:04,390
Here you are.

17
00:01:04,413 --> 00:01:06,079
Thank you.

18
00:01:06,102 --> 00:01:08,302
I'll take these for now.

19
00:01:08,325 --> 00:01:11,532
When did you arrive in Japan?

20
00:01:11,556 --> 00:01:15,322
I arrived last Friday.

21
00:01:15,345 --> 00:01:17,351
I see.

22
00:01:17,375 --> 00:01:22,648
Now, please fill out this moving-in notification form.

23
00:01:22,671 --> 00:01:24,485
Okay.

24
00:01:24,508 --> 00:01:27,766
Oh, I have a question.

25
00:01:27,790 --> 00:01:32,362
What is the 'furigana' above the name?

26
00:01:32,385 --> 00:01:36,385
That's the pronunciation of your name.

27
00:01:36,408 --> 00:01:38,411
Please write it in katakana.

28
00:01:38,435 --> 00:01:40,968
In katakana, got it.

29
00:01:40,991 --> 00:01:43,127
I see.

30
00:01:43,151 --> 00:01:47,984
Write your country's name and your current name here.

31
00:01:48,007 --> 00:01:49,578
Okay.

32
00:01:49,602 --> 00:01:52,369
Where do I write the address?

33
00:01:52,392 --> 00:01:55,792
Please write it in this large box.

34
00:01:55,814 --> 00:01:59,110
It's the address of my new apartment.

35
00:01:59,133 --> 00:02:01,023
I see.

36
00:02:01,047 --> 00:02:05,280
The kanji for the address is really difficult.

37
00:02:05,303 --> 00:02:09,336
Can I write while looking at my smartphone screen?

38
00:02:09,359 --> 00:02:12,833
Yes, of course you can.

39
00:02:12,857 --> 00:02:15,756
Take your time and write carefully.

40
00:02:15,779 --> 00:02:18,232
Thank you.

41
00:02:18,256 --> 00:02:21,432
Japanese addresses are so long!

42
00:02:21,456 --> 00:02:24,989
Do I write the room number too?

43
00:02:25,012 --> 00:02:26,587
Okay.

44
00:02:26,611 --> 00:02:31,944
Yes, please include the apartment name and room number—they're important.

45
00:02:31,967 --> 00:02:34,100
I see.

46
00:02:34,123 --> 00:02:37,400
Room 302, right?

47
00:02:37,424 --> 00:02:39,459
I've finished writing.

48
00:02:39,482 --> 00:02:41,215
Thank you.

49
00:02:41,238 --> 00:02:45,272
Please also write your date of birth and phone number here.

50
00:02:45,296 --> 00:02:49,829
I don't have a Japanese phone number yet.

51
00:02:49,852 --> 00:02:52,419
What should I do?

52
00:02:52,442 --> 00:02:54,486
I see.

53
00:02:54,509 --> 00:02:59,276
Do you have a phone number for your school or workplace?

54
00:02:59,299 --> 00:03:00,934
Okay.

55
00:03:00,958 --> 00:03:04,134
I have my Japanese language school's number.

56
00:03:04,157 --> 00:03:06,209
I'll write that down.

57
00:03:06,232 --> 00:03:09,524
Yes, that will be fine.

58
00:03:09,548 --> 00:03:11,238
All done!

59
00:03:11,262 --> 00:03:13,541
Is this everything?

60
00:03:13,564 --> 00:03:16,331
Please check this for me.

61
00:03:16,354 --> 00:03:19,120
Sure, let me see.

62
00:03:19,143 --> 00:03:24,943
Your name, address, date of birth, and school ID number, right?

63
00:03:24,966 --> 00:03:27,263
Perfect.

64
00:03:27,287 --> 00:03:29,663
Great!

65
00:03:29,686 --> 00:03:31,620
That’s a relief.

66
00:03:31,644 --> 00:03:35,012
Now, let me prepare your card.

67
00:03:35,035 --> 00:03:39,602
Please take a seat in the blue chair over there and wait.

68
00:03:39,625 --> 00:03:43,832
Okay, how long will it take?

69
00:03:43,855 --> 00:03:46,822
About 15 minutes.

70
00:03:46,845 --> 00:03:50,742
I’ll call your name when it’s ready, so please wait.

71
00:03:50,766 --> 00:03:52,569
I see.

72
00:03:52,592 --> 00:03:55,392
I’ll sit and wait.

73
00:03:55,415 --> 00:03:57,415
Thank you for waiting.

74
00:03:57,439 --> 00:04:00,206
Here’s your residence card back.

75
00:04:00,229 --> 00:04:01,847
Thank you.

76
00:04:01,871 --> 00:04:04,638
Please check the back of the card.

77
00:04:04,661 --> 00:04:08,795
Your new address is written here.

78
00:04:08,818 --> 00:04:11,754
Wow, really?

79
00:04:11,777 --> 00:04:16,453
My name and new address are both here!

80
00:04:16,477 --> 00:04:19,317
I’m so happy!

81
00:04:19,340 --> 00:04:21,174
That’s great!

82
00:04:21,197 --> 00:04:25,163
That concludes the resident registration process.

83
00:04:25,186 --> 00:04:26,820
Thank you.

84
00:04:26,843 --> 00:04:30,914
I really appreciate all your help.

85
00:04:30,938 --> 00:04:33,415
No problem at all.

86
00:04:33,438 --> 00:04:36,576
But we’re not quite done yet!

87
00:04:36,599 --> 00:04:42,268
Next, please go to the counter next door to enroll in health insurance.

88
00:04:42,292 --> 00:04:45,492
Oh, health insurance?

89
00:04:45,515 --> 00:04:47,482
I see.

90
00:04:47,505 --> 00:04:50,105
The counter next door, right?

91
00:04:50,128 --> 00:04:52,195
I’ll head over now.

92
00:04:52,217 --> 00:04:59,323
You can review today’s video with the link in the description and top comment. *Note: The site may be removed without notice.

93
00:04:59,323 --> 00:05:02,323
Scene 2: Health Insurance Enrollment Procedure

94
00:05:02,323 --> 00:05:04,756
Excuse me.

95
00:05:04,779 --> 00:05:11,462
I was told to enroll in health insurance at the next counter.

96
00:05:11,486 --> 00:05:14,185
Welcome!

97
00:05:14,209 --> 00:05:18,675
You’re here for National Health Insurance enrollment, correct?

98
00:05:18,698 --> 00:05:22,632
May I see your residence card from earlier?

99
00:05:22,655 --> 00:05:25,126
Yes, here it is.

100
00:05:25,149 --> 00:05:28,389
You already filled in your address earlier.

101
00:05:28,412 --> 00:05:30,079
Thank you.

102
00:05:30,103 --> 00:05:32,147
Let me confirm.

103
00:05:32,170 --> 00:05:37,304
Health insurance is very important for life in Japan.

104
00:05:37,326 --> 00:05:40,393
Yes, I know.

105
00:05:40,416 --> 00:05:45,216
But I don’t really understand how the insurance system works.

106
00:05:45,239 --> 00:05:47,082
No worries, I’ll explain.

107
00:05:47,106 --> 00:05:48,981
Let me explain.

108
00:05:49,004 --> 00:05:54,093
If you get sick in Japan, you’ll go to the hospital, right?

109
00:05:54,117 --> 00:05:55,650
Okay.

110
00:05:55,673 --> 00:05:59,540
Getting sick is really worrying.

111
00:05:59,564 --> 00:06:02,932
Does it cost a lot of money?

112
00:06:02,956 --> 00:06:09,189
With this health insurance card, your hospital bills will be much cheaper.

113
00:06:09,212 --> 00:06:12,709
You only pay 30% of the total cost.

114
00:06:12,732 --> 00:06:15,400
Only 30%?

115
00:06:15,424 --> 00:06:19,912
So I don’t have to pay the remaining 70%?

116
00:06:19,935 --> 00:06:23,935
Yes, the rest will be covered by the government.

117
00:06:23,958 --> 00:06:27,292
So, it's very reassuring.

118
00:06:27,315 --> 00:06:29,786
That's wonderful.

119
00:06:29,809 --> 00:06:32,463
That puts me a little more at ease.

120
00:06:32,487 --> 00:06:38,181
But I have to pay a monthly insurance premium.

121
00:06:38,204 --> 00:06:41,238
Oh, every month?

122
00:06:41,261 --> 00:06:43,757
How much is it?

123
00:06:43,780 --> 00:06:49,264
I'm an international student, so I don't have much money.

124
00:06:49,288 --> 00:06:52,154
Don't worry, it's okay.

125
00:06:52,177 --> 00:06:58,650
If your part-time income is low or you're a student, the premium gets cheaper.

126
00:06:58,674 --> 00:07:00,807
It gets cheaper?

127
00:07:00,830 --> 00:07:02,763
Great!

128
00:07:02,786 --> 00:07:06,521
Can you tell me how much it will be now?

129
00:07:06,545 --> 00:07:12,378
Since I wasn't in Japan last year, I qualify for the lowest rate.

130
00:07:12,401 --> 00:07:15,568
It's about 2,000 yen per month.

131
00:07:15,591 --> 00:07:18,265
2,000 yen a month?

132
00:07:18,288 --> 00:07:22,455
At that price, I can afford it.

133
00:07:22,478 --> 00:07:24,693
Great!

134
00:07:24,717 --> 00:07:29,599
Now, let me explain how to pay.

135
00:07:29,623 --> 00:07:31,889
Yes, please.

136
00:07:31,912 --> 00:07:35,180
Will it be automatically deducted from my bank account?

137
00:07:35,204 --> 00:07:41,887
You can set up bank payments later, but first, you'll receive a payment slip at home.

138
00:07:41,910 --> 00:07:44,527
A payment slip?

139
00:07:44,550 --> 00:07:46,962
What's that?

140
00:07:46,986 --> 00:07:50,046
It's a paper with a barcode.

141
00:07:50,069 --> 00:07:54,603
It will be mailed to your home every month.

142
00:07:54,626 --> 00:07:59,863
Where do I take this paper to pay?

143
00:07:59,887 --> 00:08:01,723
At a bank?

144
00:08:01,746 --> 00:08:08,146
You can pay at a bank, but convenience stores are the most convenient.

145
00:08:08,169 --> 00:08:11,369
You can pay anytime, 24 hours a day.

146
00:08:11,392 --> 00:08:15,392
I can pay at a convenience store?

147
00:08:15,415 --> 00:08:18,215
That's really convenient!

148
00:08:18,238 --> 00:08:24,238
Yes, just show the paper to the cashier and pay.

149
00:08:24,261 --> 00:08:28,294
Make sure to pay before the deadline.

150
00:08:28,317 --> 00:08:30,517
I see.

151
00:08:30,540 --> 00:08:34,674
I'll go to the convenience store as soon as I get the slip.

152
00:08:34,697 --> 00:08:37,030
That's great.

153
00:08:37,053 --> 00:08:41,853
Now, let's complete the procedure. Please wait a moment.

154
00:08:41,876 --> 00:08:44,209
Yes, please.

155
00:08:44,232 --> 00:08:46,365
Thank you for waiting.

156
00:08:46,388 --> 00:08:52,755
This is your National Health Insurance card.

157
00:08:52,778 --> 00:08:56,551
It has a long name, but we just call it the insurance card.

158
00:08:56,574 --> 00:08:59,210
This is the insurance card?

159
00:08:59,234 --> 00:09:02,234
It's a small card.

160
00:09:02,257 --> 00:09:04,031
Okay.

161
00:09:04,054 --> 00:09:09,054
Be sure to bring this card with you when you go to the hospital.

162
00:09:09,077 --> 00:09:12,087
It's a good idea to keep it in your wallet.

163
00:09:12,111 --> 00:09:13,758
I see.

164
00:09:13,781 --> 00:09:16,955
I'll keep it in my wallet at all times.

165
00:09:16,979 --> 00:09:20,313
You can use it starting today.

166
00:09:20,336 --> 00:09:24,913
Take care of yourself and enjoy your life in Japan.

167
00:09:24,936 --> 00:09:26,419
Okay.

168
00:09:26,443 --> 00:09:31,410
Thank you so much for your kindness and detailed explanation.

169
00:09:31,432 --> 00:09:34,832
No problem at all.

170
00:09:34,855 --> 00:09:39,624
If you ever have any trouble, feel free to come back anytime.

171
00:09:39,648 --> 00:09:42,490
Yes, I will. Thanks again.

172
00:09:42,513 --> 00:09:44,551
Excuse me.

173
00:09:44,575 --> 00:09:53,654
If you understood, please leave a comment!

174
00:09:53,654 --> 00:09:56,654
Scene 3: Opening a Bank Account

175
00:09:56,654 --> 00:09:59,134
Excuse me.

176
00:09:59,157 --> 00:10:03,976
I'd like to open a new bank account.

177
00:10:03,999 --> 00:10:05,999
Welcome.

178
00:10:06,022 --> 00:10:09,155
Opening a new account, I see.

179
00:10:09,178 --> 00:10:14,178
What will you be using this account for today?

180
00:10:14,201 --> 00:10:19,535
I need it because I'm starting a part-time job in Japan.

181
00:10:19,558 --> 00:10:21,173
I understand.

182
00:10:21,196 --> 00:10:27,045
For your part-time job salary deposits and monthly living expenses, right?

183
00:10:27,068 --> 00:10:30,354
Yes, that's right.

184
00:10:30,378 --> 00:10:36,429
My employer told me to open an account at this bank.

185
00:10:36,452 --> 00:10:38,622
Got it.

186
00:10:38,645 --> 00:10:43,423
First, let me verify your identity.

187
00:10:43,447 --> 00:10:47,724
Do you have your residence card and passport with you?

188
00:10:47,748 --> 00:10:50,518
Yes, I brought them.

189
00:10:50,542 --> 00:10:53,575
I'll take them out of my bag.

190
00:10:53,598 --> 00:10:55,845
Here you go.

191
00:10:55,868 --> 00:10:57,668
Here you are.

192
00:10:57,691 --> 00:10:59,294
Thank you.

193
00:10:59,318 --> 00:11:01,752
I'll take these for now.

194
00:11:01,775 --> 00:11:05,775
Your residence period is fine as well.

195
00:11:05,798 --> 00:11:11,642
Now, please fill in your name and address on this application form.

196
00:11:11,665 --> 00:11:13,279
Okay.

197
00:11:13,303 --> 00:11:16,403
Write it in kanji and katakana, please.

198
00:11:16,426 --> 00:11:18,598
Sure, I will.

199
00:11:18,621 --> 00:11:23,838
Oh, by the way, do you have a personal seal with you today?

200
00:11:23,862 --> 00:11:25,531
Huh?

201
00:11:25,554 --> 00:11:27,600
A seal?

202
00:11:27,624 --> 00:11:31,190
I'm sorry, I don't have it.

203
00:11:31,213 --> 00:11:33,291
What should I do?

204
00:11:33,315 --> 00:11:38,353
Can't I open an account without a seal?

205
00:11:38,376 --> 00:11:41,748
Oh, it's alright.

206
00:11:41,772 --> 00:11:44,505
Don't worry so much.

207
00:11:44,528 --> 00:11:50,528
At our branch, you can register with a signature even without a seal.

208
00:11:50,551 --> 00:11:52,751
Really?

209
00:11:52,774 --> 00:11:55,049
That’s great!

210
00:11:55,073 --> 00:11:57,342
I was really panicking.

211
00:11:57,365 --> 00:12:01,932
No worries, it's fine.

212
00:12:01,955 --> 00:12:09,760
Now, please sign your name in this square box for your registered seal.

213
00:12:09,784 --> 00:12:13,226
Should I use the same signature as on my passport?

214
00:12:13,249 --> 00:12:14,816
Okay.

215
00:12:14,839 --> 00:12:17,805
Yes, please use the same one as on your passport.

216
00:12:17,828 --> 00:12:19,795
I see.

217
00:12:19,819 --> 00:12:22,954
I've written it inside the box.

218
00:12:22,977 --> 00:12:25,344
Is this okay?

219
00:12:25,367 --> 00:12:28,985
Yes, it looks great.

220
00:12:29,009 --> 00:12:30,891
Thank you.

221
00:12:30,914 --> 00:12:35,728
Next, please set your PIN for the cash card.

222
00:12:35,752 --> 00:12:38,886
A PIN?

223
00:12:38,909 --> 00:12:41,242
What's that?

224
00:12:41,265 --> 00:12:46,398
It's a four-digit secret number you'll use with your card.

225
00:12:46,421 --> 00:12:48,438
I see.

226
00:12:48,462 --> 00:12:51,429
Four numbers, got it.

227
00:12:51,452 --> 00:12:53,028
Okay.

228
00:12:53,051 --> 00:12:59,686
Please enter the numbers twice on this machine where no one can see.

229
00:12:59,710 --> 00:13:07,756
Avoid simple numbers like your birthday or 1234, please.

230
00:13:07,780 --> 00:13:09,913
I see.

231
00:13:09,936 --> 00:13:13,829
I'll enter my secret number now.

232
00:13:13,853 --> 00:13:15,629
All done!

233
00:13:15,652 --> 00:13:17,285
Thank you.

234
00:13:17,308 --> 00:13:21,750
We'll proceed with the paperwork, so please wait over there.

235
00:13:21,774 --> 00:13:24,387
Okay, I understand.

236
00:13:24,411 --> 00:13:27,078
Sure, I will.

237
00:13:27,100 --> 00:13:29,900
Thank you for waiting.

238
00:13:29,923 --> 00:13:34,457
Here's your new passbook and cash card.

239
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:36,556
Wow, thank you so much!

240
00:13:36,579 --> 00:13:40,713
Now I can receive my part-time job salary.

241
00:13:40,736 --> 00:13:42,944
That's great!

242
00:13:42,967 --> 00:13:46,540
Good luck with your life in Japan!

243
00:13:46,563 --> 00:13:48,163
Okay.

244
00:13:48,186 --> 00:13:52,919
Thank you so much for your kindness and help!

245
00:13:52,942 --> 00:13:55,676
No problem at all.

246
00:13:55,699 --> 00:13:58,567
Please take care on your way home.

247
00:13:58,590 --> 00:14:01,590
Scene 4: SIM Card Contract Guide – Beginner’s Guide to Getting a SIM in Japan

248
00:14:01,590 --> 00:14:03,357
Excuse me.

249
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:07,380
I’d like to use a smartphone in Japan.

250
00:14:07,403 --> 00:14:11,485
Can I sign up for a new SIM card?

251
00:14:11,509 --> 00:14:13,542
Welcome.

252
00:14:13,565 --> 00:14:17,198
Of course, you can!

253
00:14:17,221 --> 00:14:21,021
You’d like to get a new SIM card, right?

254
00:14:21,044 --> 00:14:23,411
Yes, that's right.

255
00:14:23,434 --> 00:14:29,867
I just arrived in Japan, so I need a Japanese phone number.

256
00:14:29,890 --> 00:14:31,724
I see.

257
00:14:31,746 --> 00:14:38,380
First, let’s choose a data plan.

258
00:14:38,403 --> 00:14:47,650
We offer 3GB, 10GB, 30GB, and unlimited data plans.

259
00:14:47,674 --> 00:14:51,874
Uh… gigabytes?

260
00:14:51,897 --> 00:14:57,230
The plan names are confusing—I don’t really get it.

261
00:14:57,253 --> 00:15:03,220
There’s so much kanji and English… my head’s starting to hurt.

262
00:15:03,243 --> 00:15:06,981
Haha, no worries!

263
00:15:07,004 --> 00:15:09,204
It *is* confusing, isn’t it?

264
00:15:09,227 --> 00:15:11,960
Let’s take it slow.

265
00:15:11,983 --> 00:15:17,983
Do you watch a lot of YouTube or videos when you’re out?

266
00:15:18,006 --> 00:15:24,773
Yes! I watch Japanese YouTube videos every day.

267
00:15:24,796 --> 00:15:28,963
I need to study, so I want to watch anytime.

268
00:15:28,986 --> 00:15:31,319
That's great.

269
00:15:31,342 --> 00:15:39,742
In that case, 3GB or 10GB won’t be enough—you’ll run out fast.

270
00:15:39,765 --> 00:15:46,535
If you want to watch videos worry-free, the 30GB plan is your best bet.

271
00:15:46,558 --> 00:15:49,172
30GB, huh?

272
00:15:49,195 --> 00:15:52,195
That sounds reassuring.

273
00:15:52,218 --> 00:15:54,917
I’ll go with that plan.

274
00:15:54,941 --> 00:16:00,193
I’m so happy I could pick the right one myself!

275
00:16:00,216 --> 00:16:02,289
Great!

276
00:16:02,312 --> 00:16:08,346
Now, could I see your residence card for the paperwork?

277
00:16:08,369 --> 00:16:10,535
Yes, here it is.

278
00:16:10,558 --> 00:16:12,125
Here you are.

279
00:16:12,148 --> 00:16:14,046
Thank you.

280
00:16:14,069 --> 00:16:20,113
Do you have a credit card to pay the monthly fee?

281
00:16:20,136 --> 00:16:25,977
Yes, I have one from my home country—will it work?

282
00:16:26,001 --> 00:16:33,080
Yes! As long as it has one of these international brand logos, overseas cards are fine.

283
00:16:33,103 --> 00:16:35,037
Great!

284
00:16:35,060 --> 00:16:36,527
Here you go.

285
00:16:36,551 --> 00:16:37,837
Here you are.

286
00:16:37,860 --> 00:16:40,460
I'll take these for now.

287
00:16:40,483 --> 00:16:43,576
Great, I can see it works.

288
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:49,738
Now, please review the contract on this tablet.

289
00:16:49,761 --> 00:16:54,528
Whoa, there’s a lot of Japanese here.

290
00:16:54,551 --> 00:16:57,984
I’ll just explain the key points.

291
00:16:58,007 --> 00:17:03,540
The monthly fee and contract duration are listed here.

292
00:17:03,563 --> 00:17:06,207
Got it.

293
00:17:06,231 --> 00:17:08,964
The price works for me too.

294
00:17:08,987 --> 00:17:16,475
Now, please sign electronically in the box at the bottom—with your finger or a stylus.

295
00:17:16,499 --> 00:17:19,265
I write directly on the screen?

296
00:17:19,288 --> 00:17:21,767
Yes, that's right.

297
00:17:21,791 --> 00:17:24,924
Just your name is fine.

298
00:17:24,947 --> 00:17:26,781
I see.

299
00:17:26,804 --> 00:17:28,692
I've finished writing.

300
00:17:28,715 --> 00:17:30,392
Thank you.

301
00:17:30,415 --> 00:17:33,058
Alright, I’ll prepare your SIM card now.

302
00:17:33,082 --> 00:17:37,615
It’ll take about 10 minutes, so please have a seat over here.

303
00:17:37,638 --> 00:17:40,005
Got it.

304
00:17:40,028 --> 00:17:42,995
Thank you for waiting!

305
00:17:43,018 --> 00:17:47,885
I’ve inserted your new SIM card into your phone.

306
00:17:47,908 --> 00:17:53,283
Now, let’s test if the internet connects.

307
00:17:53,306 --> 00:17:55,440
Yes, please.

308
00:17:55,463 --> 00:17:58,396
This is so nerve-wracking!

309
00:17:58,419 --> 00:18:00,952
Oh, look at the screen!

310
00:18:00,975 --> 00:18:03,913
The signal bars just appeared!

311
00:18:03,937 --> 00:18:07,104
Try opening the internet.

312
00:18:07,127 --> 00:18:11,728
Wow! YouTube loaded right away!

313
00:18:11,751 --> 00:18:14,184
It’s super fast!

314
00:18:14,207 --> 00:18:17,207
The test passed—perfect!

315
00:18:17,230 --> 00:18:23,063
Now you can use a Japanese phone number and the internet starting today!

316
00:18:23,086 --> 00:18:24,886
That’s great!

317
00:18:24,909 --> 00:18:29,158
Now I can contact my friends and family right away.

318
00:18:29,181 --> 00:18:33,115
Thank you so much for your help.

319
00:18:33,138 --> 00:18:36,304
No problem at all.

320
00:18:36,327 --> 00:18:40,220
I hope you enjoy your life in Japan!

321
00:18:40,244 --> 00:18:43,244
Scene 5: Signing the Lease for Your New Apartment

322
00:18:43,244 --> 00:18:45,444
Excuse me.

323
00:18:45,467 --> 00:18:49,201
I’ve rented a new apartment.

324
00:18:49,223 --> 00:18:54,957
Today’s the big day—signing the lease and getting the keys!

325
00:18:54,980 --> 00:18:57,036
Welcome.

326
00:18:57,060 --> 00:18:59,497
We’ve been expecting you.

327
00:18:59,521 --> 00:19:02,854
You’re here to finalize the lease for your new place, right?

328
00:19:02,877 --> 00:19:06,527
Yes, please.

329
00:19:06,550 --> 00:19:09,750
I’m so excited!

330
00:19:09,773 --> 00:19:15,340
First, let’s go over the final details of your lease.

331
00:19:15,363 --> 00:19:22,218
The address is 3-1-2 Nishi-Shinjuku, Shinjuku-ku.

332
00:19:22,241 --> 00:19:27,309
The apartment is Midori-So, Room 201.

333
00:19:27,333 --> 00:19:30,420
Yes, that’s correct.

334
00:19:30,443 --> 00:19:34,076
This is going to be my new home!

335
00:19:34,099 --> 00:19:41,156
The rent is 60,000 yen per month, due by the 25th of each month.

336
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:44,387
Got it.

337
00:19:44,410 --> 00:19:48,489
I’ll set it up for automatic payment from my bank account.

338
00:19:48,513 --> 00:19:52,046
The lease term is for two years.

339
00:19:52,069 --> 00:19:58,685
If you move out before the two years are up, please notify us one month in advance.

340
00:19:58,709 --> 00:20:01,342
One month’s notice, got it.

341
00:20:01,365 --> 00:20:03,732
I see.

342
00:20:03,755 --> 00:20:07,635
Next, let’s confirm the initial costs.

343
00:20:07,659 --> 00:20:14,508
We confirmed the payment for the deposit, key money, and first month’s rent yesterday.

344
00:20:14,532 --> 00:20:19,098
Yes, I transferred it from my online bank account.

345
00:20:19,121 --> 00:20:22,210
Great, we’ve confirmed the payment.

346
00:20:22,234 --> 00:20:29,567
That concludes all the paperwork. Here are the keys to your new apartment.

347
00:20:29,590 --> 00:20:34,157
Wow, are these the keys to my place?

348
00:20:34,180 --> 00:20:37,151
I’m so happy!

349
00:20:37,174 --> 00:20:41,108
Yes, please take good care of them.

350
00:20:41,131 --> 00:20:43,897
Make sure you don’t lose them.

351
00:20:43,920 --> 00:20:47,687
I’ll keep them in my bag at all times.

352
00:20:47,710 --> 00:20:53,768
Finally, let me explain the apartment’s trash disposal rules—this is very important.

353
00:20:53,792 --> 00:20:59,089
Trash rules? That sounds serious.

354
00:20:59,112 --> 00:21:04,398
I’ve heard Japan’s trash separation rules are really strict.

355
00:21:04,422 --> 00:21:10,889
I’m a little nervous I might make a mistake.

356
00:21:10,912 --> 00:21:13,479
Don't worry, it's okay.

357
00:21:13,502 --> 00:21:16,106
Don’t worry too much!

358
00:21:16,129 --> 00:21:19,696
There are a lot of rules, that’s true.

359
00:21:19,719 --> 00:21:26,175
You’ll need to separate your trash into burnable, non-burnable, cans, and recyclables.

360
00:21:26,199 --> 00:21:31,399
Wait, there are that many categories?

361
00:21:31,422 --> 00:21:33,708
That sounds complicated.

362
00:21:33,731 --> 00:21:39,470
Also, in this town, trash pickup days are fixed.

363
00:21:39,494 --> 00:21:45,129
Burnable trash should be put out by 8 AM on Tuesdays and Fridays.

364
00:21:45,152 --> 00:21:48,249
Tuesdays and Fridays, got it.

365
00:21:48,273 --> 00:21:51,284
I’m worried I won’t remember.

366
00:21:51,307 --> 00:21:53,374
You’ll be fine!

367
00:21:53,397 --> 00:21:59,045
Also, make sure to use these clear, designated trash bags.

368
00:21:59,068 --> 00:22:02,702
You can buy them at the supermarket.

369
00:22:02,725 --> 00:22:05,263
Designated trash bags?

370
00:22:05,287 --> 00:22:08,566
Can’t I use my own bags?

371
00:22:08,589 --> 00:22:13,556
If you don’t use the designated bags, we won’t collect your trash.

372
00:22:13,579 --> 00:22:15,465
I see.

373
00:22:15,488 --> 00:22:18,622
That’s really strict, isn’t it?

374
00:22:18,645 --> 00:22:21,845
But don’t worry.

375
00:22:21,868 --> 00:22:28,301
We’ve prepared this illustrated weekly calendar just for you!

376
00:22:28,324 --> 00:22:31,857
Wow, what’s this?

377
00:22:31,880 --> 00:22:35,734
The illustrations are so cute!

378
00:22:35,758 --> 00:22:42,046
With this, you’ll know exactly which trash to take out on which day.

379
00:22:42,070 --> 00:22:44,436
That’s amazing!

380
00:22:44,459 --> 00:22:49,892
Now I won’t make any mistakes when taking out the trash.

381
00:22:49,915 --> 00:22:52,315
Great!

382
00:22:52,338 --> 00:22:55,778
It’ll be really handy if you put it up on your wall.

383
00:22:55,802 --> 00:22:57,256
Okay.

384
00:22:57,280 --> 00:23:00,213
I’ll put it up on my wall right away!

385
00:23:00,236 --> 00:23:03,878
This makes me even more excited for my new life here!

386
00:23:03,902 --> 00:23:07,469
Good luck with everything!

387
00:23:07,492 --> 00:23:11,368
And remember, if you ever need help, don’t hesitate to contact the real estate agency.

388
00:23:11,391 --> 00:23:13,263
Okay.

389
00:23:13,287 --> 00:23:15,087
Thank you.

390
00:23:15,110 --> 00:23:17,283
I’ll head over now.

391
00:23:17,307 --> 00:23:20,307
Scene 6: Starting Electricity Service

392
00:23:20,307 --> 00:23:25,798
Hello, I just moved into my apartment today.

393
00:23:25,821 --> 00:23:29,555
I’d like to set up my electricity service.

394
00:23:29,578 --> 00:23:32,631
Thank you for calling.

395
00:23:32,655 --> 00:23:36,348
This is the Tokyo Electricity Support Center.

396
00:23:36,371 --> 00:23:39,827
I see—you’re setting up new electricity service.

397
00:23:39,851 --> 00:23:42,518
Yes, that's right.

398
00:23:42,541 --> 00:23:49,382
I’m a little nervous since we can’t see each other over the phone.

399
00:23:49,405 --> 00:23:51,692
Don't worry, it's okay.

400
00:23:51,716 --> 00:23:55,887
Is my speech clear enough?

401
00:23:55,910 --> 00:23:59,284
I’ll speak slowly.

402
00:23:59,307 --> 00:24:01,604
Yes, I can understand you perfectly.

403
00:24:01,627 --> 00:24:03,394
Thank you.

404
00:24:03,417 --> 00:24:09,893
First, could you please provide your new address and name?

405
00:24:09,916 --> 00:24:20,316
My address is Apartment 201, Midori-so, 3-1-2 Nishi-Shinjuku, Shinjuku-ku.

406
00:24:20,339 --> 00:24:29,272
Apartment 201, Midori-so, 3-1-2 Nishi-Shinjuku, Shinjuku-ku—got it.

407
00:24:29,295 --> 00:24:31,295
Confirmed.

408
00:24:31,318 --> 00:24:35,086
My name is Maria.

409
00:24:35,110 --> 00:24:37,361
Maria—thank you.

410
00:24:37,384 --> 00:24:39,123
Thank you.

411
00:24:39,147 --> 00:24:44,001
Next, may I have your contact phone number?

412
00:24:44,024 --> 00:24:52,458
I don’t have a Japanese phone yet, so is it okay to use my language school’s number?

413
00:24:52,481 --> 00:24:57,540
Yes, the school’s number is fine.

414
00:24:57,563 --> 00:24:59,763
Please go ahead.

415
00:24:59,786 --> 00:25:06,192
It’s 03-1234-5678.

416
00:25:06,216 --> 00:25:08,259
Thank you.

417
00:25:08,283 --> 00:25:10,335
Registered.

418
00:25:10,358 --> 00:25:16,200
Would you like your electricity service to start today, July 9th?

419
00:25:16,224 --> 00:25:20,390
Yes, I’d like to start using it today.

420
00:25:20,413 --> 00:25:25,348
I’m in my apartment now, but the lights aren’t working.

421
00:25:25,372 --> 00:25:28,542
It’s really dark in here.

422
00:25:28,566 --> 00:25:30,232
I see.

423
00:25:30,255 --> 00:25:34,661
Let’s get your electricity working right away.

424
00:25:34,685 --> 00:25:38,019
Okay, what should I do?

425
00:25:38,042 --> 00:25:42,685
Please turn on the breaker in your apartment.

426
00:25:42,708 --> 00:25:46,475
Uh… the *breaker*?

427
00:25:46,498 --> 00:25:49,031
What's that?

428
00:25:49,054 --> 00:25:51,489
I’m not sure what that is.

429
00:25:51,512 --> 00:25:58,046
The breaker is a black box with lots of switches—it controls the electricity in your home.

430
00:25:58,069 --> 00:26:00,935
A black box?

431
00:26:00,958 --> 00:26:03,592
Where is it?

432
00:26:03,615 --> 00:26:05,748
I don’t see it.

433
00:26:05,771 --> 00:26:13,611
It’s usually on a high wall near the entrance, laundry area, or kitchen.

434
00:26:13,635 --> 00:26:16,310
Above the entrance?

435
00:26:16,333 --> 00:26:19,344
Let me check for a moment.

436
00:26:19,367 --> 00:26:23,101
Oh, there's a box here.

437
00:26:23,124 --> 00:26:26,257
Is it the box with the switch on?

438
00:26:26,280 --> 00:26:29,613
Could you open the lid?

439
00:26:29,636 --> 00:26:31,836
Yes, I've opened it.

440
00:26:31,859 --> 00:26:35,793
There are lots of small switches inside.

441
00:26:35,816 --> 00:26:40,073
Is the largest switch turned off?

442
00:26:40,096 --> 00:26:42,630
Please turn it on.

443
00:26:42,654 --> 00:26:45,187
It's off.

444
00:26:45,210 --> 00:26:48,277
Should I flip it up?

445
00:26:48,300 --> 00:26:52,306
Yes, please flip it up.

446
00:26:52,329 --> 00:26:54,339
I see.

447
00:26:54,362 --> 00:26:56,647
This is a little scary.

448
00:26:56,671 --> 00:26:58,690
Here I go.

449
00:26:58,713 --> 00:27:03,286
Alright—whoa! The lights just flickered on!

450
00:27:03,310 --> 00:27:06,276
The room is so much brighter now.

451
00:27:06,299 --> 00:27:08,533
Great!

452
00:27:08,556 --> 00:27:12,233
The power is successfully restored!

453
00:27:12,256 --> 00:27:13,825
Thank you.

454
00:27:13,848 --> 00:27:17,582
I just learned the word 'breaker' for the first time.

455
00:27:17,605 --> 00:27:21,738
I'm so impressed I could do it myself!

456
00:27:21,761 --> 00:27:26,028
Haha, I'm glad I could help.

457
00:27:26,052 --> 00:27:29,109
You can use electricity anytime from now on.

458
00:27:29,132 --> 00:27:30,703
Okay.

459
00:27:30,726 --> 00:27:36,493
Even though we talked on the phone without seeing each other, you were so kind and reassuring.

460
00:27:36,516 --> 00:27:39,370
No problem at all.

461
00:27:39,394 --> 00:27:42,760
Thank you so much, really.

462
00:27:42,783 --> 00:27:45,783
Scene 7: Water Service Activation Procedure

463
00:27:45,783 --> 00:27:47,950
Excuse me.

464
00:27:47,973 --> 00:27:50,940
Is this Minami Water Bureau?

465
00:27:50,963 --> 00:27:53,805
I just moved into a new place.

466
00:27:53,829 --> 00:27:58,162
I'd like to set up water service.

467
00:27:58,185 --> 00:28:00,785
Thank you for calling.

468
00:28:00,808 --> 00:28:04,041
This is Minami Water Bureau.

469
00:28:04,064 --> 00:28:06,798
You'd like to start water service, correct?

470
00:28:06,821 --> 00:28:09,454
Yes, that's right.

471
00:28:09,477 --> 00:28:15,810
My Japanese isn't very good yet, so I'm a little nervous.

472
00:28:15,833 --> 00:28:18,513
Don't worry, it's okay.

473
00:28:18,537 --> 00:28:21,509
I’ll speak slowly.

474
00:28:21,532 --> 00:28:27,305
First, could you please tell me your new address and name?

475
00:28:27,329 --> 00:28:34,600
The address is 3-1-2 Nishi-Shinjuku, Shinjuku-ku.

476
00:28:34,623 --> 00:28:40,664
The apartment is Midori-So, Room 201.

477
00:28:40,688 --> 00:28:49,181
Apartment 201, Midori-so, 3-1-2 Nishi-Shinjuku, Shinjuku-ku—got it.

478
00:28:49,204 --> 00:28:52,475
May I have your name, please?

479
00:28:52,499 --> 00:28:54,551
Maria.

480
00:28:54,574 --> 00:28:56,707
Maria—thank you.

481
00:28:56,730 --> 00:28:58,947
Thank you.

482
00:28:58,971 --> 00:29:01,846
Do you have a phone number?

483
00:29:01,869 --> 00:29:04,521
Yes, I have them.

484
00:29:04,545 --> 00:29:11,678
It's 090-1234-5678.

485
00:29:11,701 --> 00:29:13,669
Thank you.

486
00:29:13,692 --> 00:29:16,667
Would you like to start using the water today?

487
00:29:16,691 --> 00:29:20,424
Yes, I’d like to start using it today.

488
00:29:20,447 --> 00:29:23,489
I'm inside the apartment now.

489
00:29:23,513 --> 00:29:27,646
But I haven't turned the faucet yet.

490
00:29:27,669 --> 00:29:29,669
I see.

491
00:29:29,692 --> 00:29:34,259
Let's check it together now.

492
00:29:34,282 --> 00:29:36,848
Please go to the kitchen.

493
00:29:36,871 --> 00:29:40,738
Okay, I'm in the kitchen now.

494
00:29:40,762 --> 00:29:43,962
Turn the faucet slowly.

495
00:29:43,985 --> 00:29:46,519
Is water coming out?

496
00:29:46,542 --> 00:29:49,308
Okay, I'm turning it.

497
00:29:49,331 --> 00:29:52,343
This is so nerve-wracking!

498
00:29:52,367 --> 00:29:55,334
Oh, no water is coming out.

499
00:29:55,357 --> 00:29:57,836
What should I do?

500
00:29:57,859 --> 00:30:00,326
No water is coming out?

501
00:30:00,349 --> 00:30:04,359
Then let's check the main valve outside.

502
00:30:04,382 --> 00:30:07,382
The main valve?

503
00:30:07,405 --> 00:30:09,872
What's that?

504
00:30:09,895 --> 00:30:13,862
It refers to the outdoor water valve.

505
00:30:13,885 --> 00:30:18,528
Is there a blue box on the floor near the entrance?

506
00:30:18,551 --> 00:30:21,160
The blue box?

507
00:30:21,184 --> 00:30:24,784
I'll take a quick look outside.

508
00:30:24,807 --> 00:30:28,174
Oh, there's a blue box on the floor.

509
00:30:28,197 --> 00:30:31,063
Please open that box.

510
00:30:31,086 --> 00:30:35,020
Inside, you'll find a black round handle.

511
00:30:35,043 --> 00:30:37,939
Yes, I've opened it.

512
00:30:37,962 --> 00:30:40,653
There's a black handle inside.

513
00:30:40,677 --> 00:30:45,090
Turn that handle to the right as far as you can.

514
00:30:45,113 --> 00:30:47,195
I see.

515
00:30:47,218 --> 00:30:49,115
Turning it now.

516
00:30:49,139 --> 00:30:51,739
It's a bit stiff, isn't it?

517
00:30:51,762 --> 00:30:55,580
Ah, I've turned it all the way.

518
00:30:55,603 --> 00:30:57,261
Thank you.

519
00:30:57,285 --> 00:31:01,256
Now, please go back to the kitchen.

520
00:31:01,279 --> 00:31:04,214
Okay, I'm back.

521
00:31:04,238 --> 00:31:07,571
Please turn the faucet on again.

522
00:31:07,594 --> 00:31:10,478
Okay, I'm turning it.

523
00:31:10,502 --> 00:31:15,335
Oh! The water is gushing out now.

524
00:31:15,358 --> 00:31:17,837
I’m so happy!

525
00:31:17,861 --> 00:31:20,128
Great!

526
00:31:20,151 --> 00:31:23,027
Great, the water is running smoothly now.

527
00:31:23,050 --> 00:31:26,389
Yes, what a relief!

528
00:31:26,413 --> 00:31:29,779
Now you can enjoy fresh water.

529
00:31:29,802 --> 00:31:32,336
There's just one more step to complete.

530
00:31:32,359 --> 00:31:34,968
Please check the mailbox.

531
00:31:34,991 --> 00:31:37,058
The mailbox?

532
00:31:37,081 --> 00:31:39,566
What's inside?

533
00:31:39,590 --> 00:31:43,956
There should be a postcard labeled 'Water Service Start Application.'

534
00:31:43,979 --> 00:31:46,179
A postcard?

535
00:31:46,202 --> 00:31:49,069
Ah, I have it in my room.

536
00:31:49,092 --> 00:31:51,951
I received it from the real estate agency.

537
00:31:51,974 --> 00:31:54,741
Great!

538
00:31:54,764 --> 00:32:01,368
Please fill in today's date, your name, and address on the postcard.

539
00:32:01,392 --> 00:32:04,158
My name and address, right?

540
00:32:04,181 --> 00:32:06,018
I see.

541
00:32:06,041 --> 00:32:08,284
Go ahead and write them down.

542
00:32:08,308 --> 00:32:11,908
Then, put it in the mailbox.

543
00:32:11,931 --> 00:32:13,988
No need to go out to mail it.

544
00:32:14,011 --> 00:32:16,845
You don’t need to go out to mail it?

545
00:32:16,868 --> 00:32:18,801
That’s convenient!

546
00:32:18,824 --> 00:32:21,491
I’ll fill it out right away today.

547
00:32:21,515 --> 00:32:23,748
Sure, I will.

548
00:32:23,771 --> 00:32:27,371
That concludes today’s water service setup.

549
00:32:27,394 --> 00:32:29,878
Got it.

550
00:32:29,901 --> 00:32:34,384
Thank you so much for your kind guidance!

551
00:32:34,407 --> 00:32:37,089
No problem at all.

552
00:32:37,113 --> 00:32:40,113
I hope you enjoy your new life here!

553
00:32:40,136 --> 00:32:43,139
Yes, thank you. Goodbye!

554
00:32:43,162 --> 00:32:46,162
Scene 8: Gas Activation Inspection

555
00:32:46,162 --> 00:32:48,340
Ding-dong.

556
00:32:48,364 --> 00:32:49,657
Hello there!

557
00:32:49,680 --> 00:32:52,298
We’re from Minami Gas.

558
00:32:52,322 --> 00:32:55,993
We’re here for the gas activation inspection.

559
00:32:56,016 --> 00:32:58,216
Oh, yes!

560
00:32:58,239 --> 00:33:01,258
Ah, you’re from the gas company.

561
00:33:01,281 --> 00:33:04,048
I’ll open the door.

562
00:33:04,071 --> 00:33:05,646
Excuse me.

563
00:33:05,669 --> 00:33:08,403
I’m Yamada from Minami Gas.

564
00:33:08,426 --> 00:33:12,718
We’re here today to activate your gas service.

565
00:33:12,741 --> 00:33:15,375
Yes, I’m Maria.

566
00:33:15,398 --> 00:33:17,398
Sure, I will.

567
00:33:17,421 --> 00:33:22,718
I'm a little nervous because a stranger is coming into my room.

568
00:33:22,742 --> 00:33:25,308
Yeah, I get that.

569
00:33:25,331 --> 00:33:27,987
Sorry for making you nervous.

570
00:33:28,011 --> 00:33:31,344
I'll take off my shoes before coming in.

571
00:33:31,367 --> 00:33:33,736
Go ahead, please.

572
00:33:33,760 --> 00:33:35,766
Please come this way.

573
00:33:35,789 --> 00:33:37,462
Thank you.

574
00:33:37,486 --> 00:33:41,755
First, I'll check the gas appliances in the room.

575
00:33:41,779 --> 00:33:45,582
Where's the kitchen stove?

576
00:33:45,605 --> 00:33:48,439
The kitchen is right here.

577
00:33:48,462 --> 00:33:51,195
I'd like to use this stove.

578
00:33:51,218 --> 00:33:52,951
Thank you.

579
00:33:52,974 --> 00:33:54,851
This one, right?

580
00:33:54,875 --> 00:33:57,609
I'll inspect it for safety.

581
00:33:57,632 --> 00:34:00,250
Just a moment, please.

582
00:34:00,273 --> 00:34:03,092
Okay, I understand.

583
00:34:03,115 --> 00:34:05,649
What are you checking?

584
00:34:05,672 --> 00:34:10,205
I'm making sure the gas hose is properly connected.

585
00:34:10,228 --> 00:34:14,595
No gas leaks, so it's all good.

586
00:34:14,618 --> 00:34:17,951
Oh, that's a relief.

587
00:34:17,974 --> 00:34:22,707
Gas can be a little scary, so I feel better now.

588
00:34:22,730 --> 00:34:27,186
Yes, safety always comes first.

589
00:34:27,210 --> 00:34:31,143
Now, I'll test the stove ignition.

590
00:34:31,166 --> 00:34:34,933
Do I need to do anything?

591
00:34:34,956 --> 00:34:37,650
No, just watch.

592
00:34:37,674 --> 00:34:41,674
I'll press the switch now.

593
00:34:41,697 --> 00:34:44,300
*Click, click.*

594
00:34:44,323 --> 00:34:46,123
*Whoosh.*

595
00:34:46,146 --> 00:34:49,112
A blue flame appeared!

596
00:34:49,135 --> 00:34:51,335
Wow, that's cool!

597
00:34:51,358 --> 00:34:54,892
Yes, the flame looks nice and steady.

598
00:34:54,915 --> 00:34:57,248
The stove passes the test.

599
00:34:57,271 --> 00:35:02,238
Next, I'll check the water heater in the bathroom and washroom.

600
00:35:02,261 --> 00:35:04,794
Where's the bathroom?

601
00:35:04,817 --> 00:35:07,987
The bathroom is this way.

602
00:35:08,011 --> 00:35:09,577
Here you are.

603
00:35:09,600 --> 00:35:11,205
Excuse me.

604
00:35:11,229 --> 00:35:14,642
I'll test the hot water now.

605
00:35:14,665 --> 00:35:17,072
I'll turn on the faucet.

606
00:35:17,096 --> 00:35:19,305
Yes, please.

607
00:35:19,329 --> 00:35:22,662
I'll let the water run for a bit.

608
00:35:22,685 --> 00:35:25,218
The gas is working.

609
00:35:25,241 --> 00:35:28,441
Oh, it's turning into hot water!

610
00:35:28,464 --> 00:35:30,270
Really?

611
00:35:30,294 --> 00:35:34,227
Yes, go ahead and touch it.

612
00:35:34,250 --> 00:35:36,817
It's warm!

613
00:35:36,840 --> 00:35:39,496
Okay, I'll touch it.

614
00:35:39,519 --> 00:35:43,086
Whoa, it's really warm!

615
00:35:43,109 --> 00:35:47,042
The hot water is working perfectly.

616
00:35:47,065 --> 00:35:52,099
Yes, now you can take a warm bath every day.

617
00:35:52,122 --> 00:35:53,955
That’s great!

618
00:35:53,978 --> 00:35:58,945
Winters in Japan are cold, so I love hot water.

619
00:35:58,968 --> 00:36:01,058
That's a big relief.

620
00:36:01,082 --> 00:36:05,891
The gas safety check and hot water test are all done.

621
00:36:05,914 --> 00:36:08,281
Thank you.

622
00:36:08,304 --> 00:36:12,639
I didn't have to do anything myself, huh?

623
00:36:12,663 --> 00:36:17,432
That's right—we handle everything, so no worries.

624
00:36:17,456 --> 00:36:21,870
Finally, could you sign here, please?

625
00:36:21,894 --> 00:36:25,749
A signature? Where should I sign?

626
00:36:25,772 --> 00:36:30,505
Please write your name on the screen of this tablet.

627
00:36:30,528 --> 00:36:33,061
Confirmed.

628
00:36:33,084 --> 00:36:36,084
Scene 9: Explanation of the Missed Delivery Notice

629
00:36:36,084 --> 00:36:38,084
Excuse me.

630
00:36:38,107 --> 00:36:39,685
Hello there!

631
00:36:39,709 --> 00:36:42,394
How can I help you today?

632
00:36:42,418 --> 00:36:42,841
I found this red paper in my mailbox.

633
00:36:42,841 --> 00:36:43,264
Ah, this is a missed delivery notice.

634
00:36:43,264 --> 00:36:43,687
A missed delivery notice?

635
00:36:43,687 --> 00:36:44,110
That really surprised me.

636
00:36:44,110 --> 00:36:44,534
Did I do something wrong?

637
00:36:44,534 --> 00:36:44,957
No, not at all.

638
00:36:44,957 --> 00:36:45,380
The postal worker came by with a package while you were out.

639
00:36:45,380 --> 00:36:45,803
That’s why they left this notice in your mailbox.

640
00:36:45,803 --> 00:36:46,227
I see.

641
00:36:46,227 --> 00:36:46,650
So, it’s nothing bad, right?

642
00:36:46,650 --> 00:36:47,073
That’s a relief.

643
00:36:47,073 --> 00:36:47,496
No, it’s fine.

644
00:36:47,496 --> 00:36:47,919
Could you hand me that red notice, please?

645
00:36:47,919 --> 00:36:48,343
Go ahead, please.

646
00:36:48,343 --> 00:36:48,766
Thank you.

647
00:36:48,766 --> 00:36:49,189
I’ll check the package details.

648
00:36:49,189 --> 00:36:49,612
Oh, this is a very important document.

649
00:36:49,612 --> 00:36:50,036
An important document?

650
00:36:50,036 --> 00:36:50,459
What is it?

651
00:36:50,459 --> 00:36:50,882
This is from the Immigration Bureau.

652
00:36:50,882 --> 00:36:51,305
I need to verify your identity.

653
00:36:51,305 --> 00:36:51,728
Do you have your passport with you?

654
00:36:51,728 --> 00:36:52,152
Yes, it’s in my bag.

655
00:36:52,152 --> 00:36:52,575
I’ll take it out.

656
00:36:52,575 --> 00:36:52,998
Here you go.

657
00:36:52,998 --> 00:36:53,421
Here you are.

658
00:36:53,421 --> 00:36:53,845
Thank you.

659
00:36:53,845 --> 00:36:54,268
Let me confirm your name.

660
00:36:54,268 --> 00:36:54,691
Is your name Maria?

661
00:36:54,691 --> 00:36:55,114
Yes, I’m Maria.

662
00:36:55,114 --> 00:36:55,537
And is your address in Shinjuku?

663
00:36:55,537 --> 00:36:55,961
Yes, it’s in Shinjuku.

664
00:36:55,961 --> 00:36:56,384
Great, I can see it works.

665
00:36:56,384 --> 00:36:56,807
Here’s your passport back.

666
00:36:56,807 --> 00:36:57,230
Thank you.

667
00:36:57,230 --> 00:36:57,653
Now, please sign here.

668
00:36:57,653 --> 00:36:58,077
A signature?

669
00:36:58,077 --> 00:36:58,500
Where should I write it?

670
00:36:58,500 --> 00:36:58,923
Please sign right here on this white form.

671
00:36:58,923 --> 00:36:59,346
Should I write my name in English?

672
00:36:59,346 --> 00:36:59,770
Or in katakana?

673
00:36:59,770 --> 00:37:00,193
Please write the same name as in your passport.

674
00:37:00,193 --> 00:37:00,616
I see.

675
00:37:00,616 --> 00:37:01,039
I’ll write it here.

676
00:37:01,039 --> 00:37:01,462
All done!

677
00:37:01,462 --> 00:37:01,886
Thank you very much.

678
00:37:01,886 --> 00:37:02,309
I’ll go get your package now.

679
00:37:02,309 --> 00:37:02,732
Just a moment, please.

680
00:37:02,732 --> 00:37:03,155
Okay, I understand.

681
00:37:03,155 --> 00:37:03,579
Thank you for waiting.

682
00:37:03,579 --> 00:37:04,002
Here’s the blue envelope.

683
00:37:04,002 --> 00:37:04,425
Here you are.

684
00:37:04,425 --> 00:37:04,848
Thank you.

685
00:37:04,848 --> 00:37:05,271
Oh, there’s a card inside.

686
00:37:05,271 --> 00:37:05,695
Is this my residence card?

687
00:37:05,695 --> 00:37:06,118
Yes, that’s right.

688
00:37:06,118 --> 00:37:06,541
This is a very important card, so please keep it safe.

689
00:37:06,541 --> 00:37:06,964
Got it.

690
00:37:06,964 --> 00:37:07,388
I’ll carry it with me from today.

691
00:37:07,388 --> 00:37:07,811
Your life in Japan starts today, doesn’t it?

692
00:37:07,811 --> 00:37:08,234
Good luck!

693
00:37:08,234 --> 00:37:08,657
Thank you very much.

694
00:37:08,657 --> 00:37:09,080
The postal worker was so kind.

695
00:37:09,080 --> 00:37:09,504
I’m really happy about that.

696
00:37:09,504 --> 00:37:09,927
No problem at all.

697
00:37:09,927 --> 00:37:10,350
Goodbye.

698
00:37:10,350 --> 00:37:10,850
Goodbye.